course: dictionary
lesson: 2586
title: Dense: thick, heavy, or slow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dense has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one fits. When you see «a dense forest» or «dense fog», dense means thick, with things packed closely together. You cannot see through a dense fog because the tiny drops fill the air.
explain: In science, dense means having a lot of mass packed into a small space. Dense things feel heavy for their size. «Hot air and smoke are less dense than cool air, so they rise like a hot-air balloon.» The clue is the rising: lighter, less dense things go up.
explain: Dense can also be informal and unkind, meaning slow to understand. If a friend says, «You are so dense, you missed the joke!», they are being rude, not describing a forest. Always check the sentence around the word before you choose a meaning.
fact: Dense means thick, with things packed closely together.
fact: Dense in science means having a lot of mass packed into a small space.
fact: An object floats if it is less dense than water, and sinks if it is denser.
fact: Informal and unkind: dense can mean slow to understand.
fact: Phrases to remember: dense fog, dense forest, dense crowd, a dense population.
exercise: In «a dense forest», what does dense mean? | *Thick, with things packed closely together | Tall and thin | Bright and sunny | Empty and quiet
exercise: Why does a wooden block float on water? | It is denser than water | It is painted a light colour | *It is less dense than water | It is very hot
exercise: Nadia says, «Sam is so dense he didn't get the joke.» What does dense mean here? | Very thick and heavy | Packed closely together | *Slow to understand | Full of light
test: «Most of the gas fell to the centre, and when it became hot and dense enough, fusion switched on and the Sun was born.» In this sentence, what does dense mean? | Full of holes and gaps | Slow to understand | *Having a lot of mass packed into a small space | Cold and wet
test: Which phrase means many people living close together? | a dense fog | *a dense population | a bright lamp | a dense forest
exam: From a stile they look back at the wood, «dense, menacing, compact», what does dense suggest about the wood? | *Thick and packed closely together, so it feels threatening | Light and airy, like a summer meadow | Empty and easy to walk through | Wet and cold after rain
